WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:10.870
Reactome is a free open source, curated, and
peer-reviewed knowledgebase of biomolecular

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:12.210
pathways.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:17.500
This tool enables users to browse and perform
pathway analysis, and overlay their own data

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.890
on top of the diagrams.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:23.140
The pathway browser consists of several components.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:27.570
A species selector and other options are placed
on the top.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:30.450
The event hierarchy is on the left.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:35.649
The details panel is at the bottom and it
includes six tabs: description, molecules,

00:00:35.649 --> 00:00:39.180
structures, expression, analysis, and downloads.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.810
Finally, the viewport at the center of the
screen displays the pathways overview and

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.950
the diagram viewer.

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:50.840
The event hierarchy can be used to browse
through pathways and reactions.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:54.810
All components in the browser are tightly
connected and respond to each other's actions

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:58.120
such as hovering over items or their selection.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:02.350
The search feature in the pathway overview
can be used to find a specific pathway by

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:03.940
its name.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:08.570
Clicking on one of the search results select
the item and causes an update of every component

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:10.220
of the viewer.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:14.290
Clicking on the diagram icon opens the diagram
view.

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:20.240
When the diagram opens the location of sub
pathways are highlighted by shaded boxes.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:25.570
Selecting the fireworks like icon brings the
pathway overview back to the viewport.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:29.920
Selecting a reaction on the event hierarchy
opens the containing pathway and zooms in

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:33.320
to focus on the selected reaction.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:37.619
Transitions between the overview and pathway
diagrams are animated.

00:01:37.619 --> 00:01:41.909
Once an item is selected, detailed information
is available in the different tabs of the

00:01:41.909 --> 00:01:43.850
details panel.

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:49.030
• The description tab shows curated information
stored in the reactome database.

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:53.780
• The molecules tab provides information
about the participating molecules.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:58.360
• The structures tab shows structural information
from third-party resources.

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:05.470
Querying protein databank for proteins, ChEBI
for chemicals, and Rhea for reactions.

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:09.649
• The expression tab retrieves data from
the expression Atlas across a standard set

00:02:09.649 --> 00:02:11.980
of tissues and organs.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:17.370
• The Downloads tab shows buttons to download
the pathway in several formats for reuse or

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.489
reference.

00:02:18.489 --> 00:02:22.959
The user can control the level of information
by zooming in and out.

00:02:22.959 --> 00:02:27.569
Initially all trivial molecules are hidden
and shaded boxes highlight the locations of

00:02:27.569 --> 00:02:29.620
sub pathways.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:34.359
As the view zooms in, the trivial molecules
progressively appear while the shaded boxes

00:02:34.359 --> 00:02:36.049
fade out.

00:02:36.049 --> 00:02:40.680
As zooming continues, stoichiometry and PTMs
are shown.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:45.200
When fully zoomed, in the shapes representing
proteins and chemicals reveal their molecular

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.469
structures and associated information.

00:02:48.469 --> 00:02:53.840
When the mouse pointer is hovered over an
entity, a small triangle appears inside it.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:58.469
Clicking the triangle or right-clicking on
the entity itself opens a context dialog with

00:02:58.469 --> 00:03:03.069
more information such as its participating
molecules and other pathways where this entity

00:03:03.069 --> 00:03:04.700
occurs.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:09.680
Three buttons at the top right corner control
toggling for names to identifies.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:14.120
Pinning the contacts dialog box to the view
or closing it.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:18.689
The search feature in the diagram viewer can
be used to find entities events or interactors

00:03:18.689 --> 00:03:21.540
within the displayed pathway.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:27.230
Selecting a result in the search makes the
view smoothly transition to the area of interest.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:31.730
Different color profiles can be selected in
order to change the appearance of the displayed

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:32.819
diagram.

00:03:32.819 --> 00:03:37.040
Clicking on the red circle at the top-right
corner of an entity reveals its interactors

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:40.709
from the intact database in a radial layout.

00:03:40.709 --> 00:03:45.719
More information can be found in the interactors
tab in the context dialog.

00:03:45.719 --> 00:03:50.689
When fully zoomed in, the interactor shapes
reveal their molecular structures and associated

00:03:50.689 --> 00:03:52.809
information.

00:03:52.809 --> 00:03:56.909
Interactors can be filtered by confidence
score using the slider.

00:03:56.909 --> 00:04:02.290
Different color profiles can be selected to
change the appearance of the displayed interactors.

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:07.180
More interactive resources can be selected
in the settings panel to facilitate easy navigating

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.370
between resources.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:14.040
The revealed interactors layout is remembered
when a source is reselected.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:18.979
The pathway browser enables users to import
an overlay and their own data as a custom

00:04:18.979 --> 00:04:20.650
resource.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:25.840
The inline documentation provides more information
about the custom resources.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:30.170
The different ways of submitting the data
and the supported formats.

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:35.180
Once uploaded custom resources will remain
available for at least seven days.

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:39.600
This period of time is automatically extended
by frequent usage.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:45.090
The last part of this introductory video is
about the analysis of user data.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:49.810
Different kinds of data can be submitted via
the analysis submission interface.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:53.870
There are three steps to the analysis submission
process.

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:57.970
Selection of the data to be analyzed, setting
the available options, and performing the

00:04:57.970 --> 00:04:59.590
analysis.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:03.400
Inline documentation is also available.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:07.930
Results are displayed in the analysis tab
of the details panel and overlaid on the pathways

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:12.220
overview providing a bird's-eye view to facilitate
browsing.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:16.840
The color of the overlay indicates the significance
of the pathway match.

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:21.220
When a pathway is selected, a marker indicates
its expression level on the right side of

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.100
the scale.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:27.500
Hovering the mouse pointer over another pathway
places a marker on the left side of the expression

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:30.280
scale, allowing comparison.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:35.960
Analysis results overlaid on to pathway diagrams,
enable navigation through a series of submitted

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:39.310
expression samples such as a time series.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:44.620
In pathway diagrams entities that were represented
in the submitted dataset are colored.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:48.930
Granularity of the overlay increases with
the level of zoom.

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:53.770
When zoomed in, complexes and sets are overlaid
with colored strips to indicate the expression

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:56.630
of their participating molecules.

00:05:56.630 --> 00:06:00.660
When interactors have been included in the
analysis, if an interactive an entity has

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:04.560
been hit by the sample, a ribbon is shown
on the entity.

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:08.390
When the interactors are revealed, those that
were hit are colored on the View and in the

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:10.800
context dialog.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:19.750
Different analysis color profiles can be selected
to change the appearance of the results overlay.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:24.290
The pathway browser provides a variety of
options to export the analysis results as

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:25.599
an image or a file.

